/T (User management decides who can access an application and what each person may see and do within it. Users are added to an application and associated with permission sets \(profiles\) and roles; together these control access to forms, reports, pages and records. In the Settings area, the User Permissions section groups these controls under three tabs: Permissions, Roles and Data Sharing.)
/E (User management decides who can access an application and what each person may see and do within it. Users are added to an application and associated with permission sets \(profiles\) and roles; together these control access to forms, reports, pages and records. In the Settings area, the User Permissions section groups these controls under three tabs: Permissions, Roles and Data Sharing.)
/Pg 11 0 R
