/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 105 0 R
/T (RBAC is an access-control model in which rights are assigned to roles instead of individual users, and users acquire rights through the roles they hold. It simplifies administration, supports the principle of least privilege, improves data security, and keeps the access policy consistent and easy to audit.)
/E (RBAC is an access-control model in which rights are assigned to roles instead of individual users, and users acquire rights through the roles they hold. It simplifies administration, supports the principle of least privilege, improves data security, and keeps the access policy consistent and easy to audit.)
