/Title (User management decides who can access an application and what each person may see and do within it. Users are added to an application and associated with permission sets \(profiles\) and roles; together these control access to forms, reports, pages and records. In the Settings area, the User Permissions section groups these controls under three tabs: Permissions, Roles and Data Sharing.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 713 0 R
>>
endobj
741 0 obj
<<
/Title (RBAC is an access-control model in which rights are assigned to roles instead of individual users, and users acquire rights through the roles they hold. It simplifies administration, supports the principle of least privilege, improves data security, and keeps the access policy consistent and easy to audit.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 714 0 R
>>
endobj
